.\"
.\" clip_gpt(1) - keep in sync with src/cli.rs (USAGE) and
.\" config.toml.example; tests in src/cli.rs and src/configfile.rs check
.\" the options, config keys and defaults.
.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt CLIP_GPT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clip_gpt
.Nd rewrite the clipboard text, or read an image's text, with an LLM
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl p Ar profile Ns Op , Ns Ar profile ...
.Op Fl \-timeout Ar seconds
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar profile Ns Op , Ns Ar profile ...
.Fl \-show\-profile
.Nm
.Fl \-list\-profiles
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the text on the clipboard, sends it to an OpenAI-compatible chat
completions API (OpenAI itself, or a local server such as Ollama or
llama.cpp) together with a configurable prompt, and replaces the clipboard
contents with the response.
Settings come from named profiles in a configuration file (see
.Sx PROFILES ) ,
so different hotkeys can use different servers, models or prompts.
An image on the clipboard is sent to the model instead when there is no
text (see
.Sx IMAGES ) .
It runs once and exits; it is meant to be bound to a desktop hotkey or a
macro key rather than run interactively.
.Pp
A short high beep
.Pq Cm beep_tone
plays when the response is on the clipboard, a low one
.Pq Cm error_tone
when anything fails or the clipboard text was refused.
Messages go to standard error.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar list , Fl \-profile Ar list , Fl \-profile Ns = Ns Ar list
Use the profiles in the comma-separated
.Ar list
instead of
.Bq default .
Each kind of clipboard content goes to the last profile in the list whose
.Cm input
accepts it; see
.Sx PROFILES .
An unknown profile, an empty or repeated name, a profile with
.Ql input = [\(dqnone\(dq] ,
or giving the option twice is an error.
A listed profile that ends up handling nothing, because later ones take
every kind it accepts, only prints a warning.
.It Fl \-list\-profiles
Print the names of all profiles in the configuration file, one per line,
and exit.
.It Fl \-show\-profile
Print the settings of the selected profiles (the default one, or those
given with
.Fl p )
after includes, each with the profile it came from or
.Ql built-in default ,
and which profile handles which kind of content, then exit.
The API key is only shown as set or not.
The whole file is checked as for a normal run, so this also tests a
configuration.
.It Fl s , Fl \-no\-secret\-check
Do not refuse clipboard text that looks like an API key, token, private
key or URL with a password, for this run.
The password-manager and hidden-character checks still apply.
.It Fl \-timeout Ar seconds , Fl \-timeout Ns = Ns Ar seconds
Wait at most
.Ar seconds
for the LLM's whole answer;
.Ar 0
means no limit.
Overrides
.Cm request_timeout
for this run.
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.El
.Pp
Any other argument is an error.
.Fl s
and
.Fl \-timeout
apply to whichever profile handles the clipboard.
The argument
.Fl \-x11\-clipboard\-owner
is internal (see
.Sx CLIPBOARD )
and must not be used directly.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from a TOML file, looked up first at
.Pa ~/.config/clipgpt/config.toml
.Po
.Pa ~/Library/Application Support/clipgpt/config.toml
on macOS,
.Pa %APPDATA%\eclipgpt\econfig.toml
on Windows
.Pc
and then at
.Pa ./config.toml .
The
.Pa config.ini
of clipGPT 0.5 and older is not read.
Every table
.Bq Ar name
in the file is a profile; settings outside a table are an error.
If any profile contains a non-empty
.Cm api_key ,
the file must not be accessible by other users (mode 0600), or
.Nm
refuses to run:
.Pp
.Dl $ chmod 600 ~/.config/clipgpt/config.toml
.Pp
The whole file is checked on every run, including profiles that are not
used: an unknown key (keys are case-sensitive), a value of the wrong type,
an include of an unknown profile or an include cycle is an error.
Error messages never quote setting values.
Strings are written in double quotes, in which
.Ql \en
is a newline, or in single quotes, which take no escapes;
.Ql \(dq\(dq
is a real empty string.
Numbers and the booleans
.Ql true
and
.Ql false
are written without quotes.
.Pp
Keys, all optional unless stated:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm include
A list of profiles to start from, e.g.\&
.Ql include = [\(dqbase\(dq, \(dqbeeps\(dq] .
They are applied in order, later ones overriding earlier ones, and the
profile's own keys override them all.
Included profiles may include others.
.It Cm clear
A list of keys whose values from
.Cm include
are dropped, so the built-in default applies again, e.g.\&
.Ql clear = [\(dqapi_key\(dq, \(dqinput\(dq] .
Listing an unknown key,
.Cm include ,
.Cm clear ,
or a key the same profile sets, is an error.
.It Cm input
The kinds of clipboard content the profile handles: a list of
.Ql text
and
.Ql image ,
or
.Ql [\(dqnone\(dq]
for a profile that handles nothing and only exists to be included by
others (such a profile cannot be selected, and needs no
.Cm model ) .
Without
.Cm input
a profile handles every kind, including kinds added in later versions.
Like any other key it is passed on by
.Cm include ;
a profile that includes a
.Ql none
profile sets its own
.Cm input
or lists it in
.Cm clear .
.It Cm model
Required in every profile that handles input (set there or included).
The model name, e.g.\&
.Ql gpt-4o-mini
for OpenAI or a local model name for Ollama.
.It Cm api_url
Chat completions endpoint; default
.Ql https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions .
Only
.Ql http
and
.Ql https
are accepted; plain http to a host other than this computer prints a
warning.
.It Cm api_key
Optional bearer token.
Empty or missing means no key is sent (e.g.\& for a local Ollama), so
.Ql api_key = \(dq\(dq
also drops an included key.
.It Cm api_type
Only
.Ql OpenAI
(the default) is supported.
.It Cm prompt_text
Prompt sent as the system message; the clipboard text is sent separately
as the user message.
.It Cm prompt_image
Prompt sent as the system message when the clipboard holds an image and
no text; the image is sent separately as the user message.
The default makes the model transcribe the text in the image as Markdown,
like an OCR program.
The model must accept images; see
.Sx IMAGES .
.It Cm beep_tone
Success beep frequency in Hz; default 1046.
.It Cm error_tone
Error beep frequency in Hz; default 131.
.It Cm beep_duration
Beep length in milliseconds; default 250, 0 disables the beeps.
.It Cm max_input_bytes
Largest clipboard text, in UTF-8 bytes, that is sent; default 65536.
Larger clipboards are refused.
.It Cm max_image_bytes
Largest clipboard image, in bytes, that is sent, checked both as read and
after conversion to PNG; default 10485760.
Larger images are refused.
.It Cm allow_redirects
Follow HTTP redirects from
.Cm api_url ,
each hop checked like
.Cm api_url
itself, at most 10; default false.
.It Cm secret_check
Refuse clipboard text that looks like a secret; default true.
.It Cm request_timeout
Longest wait in whole seconds for the LLM's answer, from sending the
request to the end of the response; default 30, 0 means no limit.
Raise it for slow local models.
.El
.Sh PROFILES
Without
.Fl p ,
.Nm
uses the profile
.Bq default ;
if there is none, a profile must be given with
.Fl p .
With
.Fl p Ar a,b ,
each kind of clipboard content goes to the last listed profile whose
.Cm input
accepts it, and all settings of the run (server, model, prompt, size
limit, secret check, timeout, beeps) come from that profile.
For example, with
.Ql \-p default,ocr ,
where
.Bq ocr
has
.Ql input = [\(dqimage\(dq] ,
images go to
.Bq ocr
and text to
.Bq default ;
with
.Ql \-p ocr,default
everything goes to
.Bq default ,
and a warning says that
.Bq ocr
handles nothing.
.Pp
Only kinds some selected profile handles are read from the clipboard: if
none takes text, an image is used even when text is offered too.
Content that no selected profile accepts is refused with the error tone
and the clipboard is left unchanged.
Errors before the kind of content is known use the beeps of the last
selected profile.
.Sh CLIPBOARD
On Linux and
.Fx
the Wayland clipboard is used when the compositor
supports the ext-data-control or wlr-data-control protocol (KDE Plasma,
Sway, Hyprland and others).
Otherwise, if
.Ev DISPLAY
is set, the X11 clipboard is used: on GNOME through Xwayland, which keeps
it in sync with the Wayland clipboard, and in plain X11 sessions.
.Pp
An X11 clipboard is served by the program that set it, so after writing
the response
.Nm
leaves a copy of itself running in the background as
.Ql clip_gpt \-\-x11\-clipboard\-owner .
It exits as soon as anything else is copied.
.Sh IMAGES
If the clipboard holds no text (or only white space) but an image,
the image is sent instead, with
.Cm prompt_image .
PNG and JPEG images are sent as they are; WebP, GIF (first frame), BMP,
Windows bitmaps and TIFF are converted to PNG first.
Images to convert that are over 8192 pixels wide or high are refused.
If the clipboard holds neither text nor an image,
.Nm
plays the error tone and leaves the clipboard unchanged.
.Pp
Which model can see images is up to the configuration: there is no check
in advance.
A server or model that does not accept images answers with an HTTP error,
reported with a hint and the error tone.
For llama.cpp's
.Ql llama\-server ,
load the model with its multimodal projector
.Pq Fl \-mmproj ,
otherwise image requests fail.
Some older Ollama versions silently ignore the image instead; the answer
is then not based on it.
.Sh SECURITY
Clipboard contents marked as secret by a password manager
.Po
.Ql x\-kde\-passwordManagerHint
on Wayland and X11,
.Ql org.nspasteboard.ConcealedType
on macOS
.Pc
are never read or sent; the clipboard is replaced by a notice.
Text containing invisible Unicode tag characters is refused the same way.
Unless
.Fl s
or
.Ql secret_check = false
is used, text that looks like an API key, token, private key, JSON Web
Token or URL with a password is refused and the clipboard left as it was.
Control, bidirectional-override and zero-width characters are removed
from both the text sent and the response pasted.
Text inside an image cannot be checked this way; the model is told not to
follow instructions found in it.
Responses over 1 MiB are discarded, and error messages never include the
response body.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev HOME
Used to find
.Pa ~/.config/clipgpt/config.toml .
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland compositor to use.
.It Ev DISPLAY
The X11 display used when Wayland clipboard access is not available.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/clipgpt/config.toml
Configuration file.
.It Pa ./config.toml
Used if the file above does not exist.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the response is on the clipboard, or after
.Fl h ,
.Fl V ,
.Fl \-list\-profiles
or
.Fl \-show\-profile
with a valid configuration.
It exits 1 on any error, including an invalid option or configuration, a
failed request, and refused clipboard contents (password, hidden
characters, secret, too large, unsupported image, empty clipboard, content
no selected profile accepts).
.Sh EXAMPLES
A configuration with OpenAI for text, a local llama.cpp server with a
vision model for reading text off screenshots, and shared beeps:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ llama\-server \-hf ggml\-org/gemma\-3\-4b\-it\-GGUF

[beeps]
input = ["none"]
beep_tone = 880
beep_duration = 150

[default]
include = ["beeps"]
clear = ["input"]
api_key = "sk\-..."
model = "gpt\-4o\-mini"
prompt_text = "Fix spelling and grammar. Reply with the text only."

[ocr]
include = ["beeps"]
input = ["image"]
api_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions"
model = "gemma\-3\-4b\-it"
request_timeout = 120
.Ed
.Pp
Text to OpenAI, images to the local server:
.Pp
.Dl $ clip_gpt \-p default,ocr
.Pp
Check which profile would handle what, and with which settings:
.Pp
.Dl $ clip_gpt \-p default,ocr \-\-show\-profile
.Pp
Rewrite the clipboard once, waiting as long as the model needs:
.Pp
.Dl $ clip_gpt \-\-timeout 0
